# Getting Started

## Prerequisites

Install:

-   Python 3.10+
-   Node.js + npm
-   Git
-   Docker Desktop
-   MongoDB Atlas or local MongoDB
-   Groq API key

------------------------------------------------------------------------

## 1. Clone

``` powershell
git clone https://github.com/Om-roy14/SIH2026_Team_jagruk_swadesh.git
cd SIH2026_Team_jagruk_swadesh
```

## 2. Python Environment

``` powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Install Python packages:

``` powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment Variables

## AI / Groq

Create:

``` text
jagruk_brain_pipeline/.env
```

``` env
API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
```

Never commit the real key.

## Express / MongoDB

Create:

``` text
sihFrontend/server/.env
```

Example:

``` env
MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=replace_with_a_long_random_secret
PORT=5000
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173
FASTAPI_HOST=127.0.0.1
FASTAPI_PORT=8000
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Start Qdrant

The repository provides:

``` text
RAG/docker_compose.yml
```

Run:

``` powershell
cd RAG
docker compose -f docker_compose.yml up -d
```

Qdrant:

``` text
http://localhost:6333
```

Check:

``` powershell
docker ps
```

Stop:

``` powershell
docker compose -f docker_compose.yml down
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build / Rebuild the RAG Index

Ensure your dataset exists and update `DATA_DIR` in `RAG/index.py`.

Then:

``` powershell
python RAG/index.py
```

This creates/rebuilds:

``` text
bis_knowledge
```

in Qdrant.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Install Frontend Dependencies

``` powershell
cd sihFrontend
npm install
```

Install Express dependencies:

``` powershell
cd server
npm install
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Running the Application

## Recommended Windows Method

Run services in separate terminals.

### Terminal 1 --- Qdrant

``` powershell
cd RAG
docker compose -f docker_compose.yml up
```

### Terminal 2 --- FastAPI

From repository root:

``` powershell
python -m uvicorn fastapi_server:server --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --app-dir .
```

FastAPI:

``` text
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

### Terminal 3 --- Express

``` powershell
cd sihFrontend/server
npm run dev
```

Express:

``` text
http://localhost:5000
```

### Terminal 4 --- React

``` powershell
cd sihFrontend
npm run dev:frontend
```

Vite normally exposes:

``` text
http://localhost:5173
```

Use the exact URL printed by Vite.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# One-command Development Mode

The frontend `package.json` includes:

``` powershell
cd sihFrontend
npm run dev
```

This uses `concurrently` to start:

``` text
Express
FastAPI
Vite
```

The current script uses Uvicorn reload mode. If reload causes Windows
process lifecycle problems, use the separate-terminal method above and
start FastAPI without `--reload`.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Service Map

  Service      Default URL               Purpose
  ------------ ------------------------- ----------------------
  React/Vite   `http://localhost:5173`   Web UI
  Express      `http://localhost:5000`   Auth/API proxy
  FastAPI      `http://127.0.0.1:8000`   AI/RAG/STT/TTS
  Qdrant       `http://localhost:6333`   Vector database
  MongoDB      Atlas/local               Application database

